cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenEnergy, please cite it as below, and credit the data sources each result lists."
type: software
title: "OpenEnergy: backtest battery storage and renewables against real power-market data"
version: 5.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Koul
    given-names: Akhilesh
repository-code: "https://github.com/koulakhilesh/OpenEnergy"
url: "https://koulakhilesh.github.io/OpenEnergy/"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Python toolkit and web app that backtests grid batteries against GB
  day-ahead prices without lookahead, stacks frequency-response revenue, rebuilds GB
  prices from plant, fuel and carbon data, and applies NESO Future Energy Scenarios with
  price-taking interconnectors.
keywords:
  - energy storage
  - battery
  - electricity markets
  - backtesting
  - power systems
  - Great Britain
